<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand Embassy of Peter the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1697">1697</a>–<a href="/years/1698">1698</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grand Embassy was a Russian diplomatic mission to western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> in 1697–1698, formally led by Franz Lefort and Fyodor Golovin, in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Peter I travelled incognito as Pyotr Mikhailov. It sought allies against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and recruited specialists, while Peter studied shipbuilding at Zaandam, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> and Deptford. He cut it short to deal with the streltsy revolt of 1698, returning determined to westernise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grand-embassy-of-peter-the-great.jpg" alt="Grand Embassy of Peter the Great" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flämische Schule Ende des 17. Jahrhunderts · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Member_of_Grand_Embassy_of_Peter_the_Great_by_Flemish_anonim_(1687,_priv.coll).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
